WEBVTT

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:07.850
A boardinghouse.

00:00:07.850 --> 00:00:09.260
A tea hall.

00:00:09.870 --> 00:00:11.520
Rose parties.

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:12.860
Secret meetings.

00:00:12.860 --> 00:00:14.160
Séances.

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:17.340
A window that peers out from the library.

00:00:19.550 --> 00:00:23.080
This is bad. I'm in love.

00:00:54.940 --> 00:00:56.600
What are you doing?

00:00:56.600 --> 00:00:59.940
Oh, I just...

00:01:00.610 --> 00:01:01.990
Where are your friends?

00:01:01.990 --> 00:01:04.740
They went to check out the chapel.

00:01:04.740 --> 00:01:06.510
You didn't go with them?

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:08.440
That's right.

00:01:08.440 --> 00:01:13.750
Umm... I want to talk to
you about something...

00:01:13.750 --> 00:01:15.800
I didn't have a chance to tell you earlier...

00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:19.850
Umm...

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:22.590
You want to talk to me, huh?

00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:24.290
Can we do it outside?

00:01:24.290 --> 00:01:25.350
Huh?

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:29.720
I'd rather talk outside.

00:02:58.070 --> 00:02:59.610
That was amazing!

00:02:59.610 --> 00:03:02.030
It really was!

00:03:02.030 --> 00:03:05.230
The ceiling was so high... It was
like looking into the sky!

00:03:05.230 --> 00:03:08.050
The stained-glass windows were gorgeous!

00:03:08.050 --> 00:03:11.990
It made me hesitant to
talk too loud in there.

00:03:11.990 --> 00:03:12.930
I know, right?

00:03:12.930 --> 00:03:16.530
I'm not used to that sort of place either.

00:03:19.250 --> 00:03:25.550
I'm sorry. I screwed up and thought I
was signing up for the Literary Club.

00:03:26.570 --> 00:03:30.240
Oh. You're quitting the basketball team.

00:03:31.490 --> 00:03:34.600
What a waste. You've got
such a good body for it.

00:03:34.600 --> 00:03:36.480
I'm just tall.

00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:39.850
What a shame.

00:03:39.850 --> 00:03:41.950
A real shame.

00:03:42.460 --> 00:03:46.740
No, I'm really not athletic at all.

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:50.330
I mean it's a shame that is
where we part ways.

00:03:50.920 --> 00:03:54.050
I really liked you.

00:03:54.050 --> 00:03:55.080
Huh?

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:01.630
I realized it the second I saw you...

00:04:01.630 --> 00:04:04.240
Like, "Oh, she's my type."

00:04:05.870 --> 00:04:08.090
Don't joke like that.

00:04:08.090 --> 00:04:10.530
I'm dead serious.

00:04:18.130 --> 00:04:21.250
Wow, something special's happening
between those two.

00:04:21.250 --> 00:04:22.140
Seriously.

00:04:22.140 --> 00:04:23.380
OK, let's interrupt 'em.

00:04:23.380 --> 00:04:25.160
Why would we do that?

00:04:25.160 --> 00:04:32.110
We're already staring. All that's left
is to actually get in their way.

00:04:32.110 --> 00:04:33.390
I'm going in.

00:04:33.750 --> 00:04:37.370
Manjome-san! Let's go home!

00:04:46.380 --> 00:04:50.410
Bye-bye, Achan!

00:04:58.590 --> 00:05:01.980
She's Sugimoto-sempai.

00:05:25.540 --> 00:05:27.970
Mom!

00:05:32.020 --> 00:05:35.340
It's me, Kyoko! I'm right here!

00:05:59.560 --> 00:06:01.830
Ikumi

00:06:02.330 --> 00:06:04.790
Good morning. It's Ko.

00:06:05.850 --> 00:06:08.420
Kyoko-san, are you not ready yet?

00:06:08.870 --> 00:06:12.170
Can you wait just another minute?

00:06:12.170 --> 00:06:14.550
Sorry to make you wait, Ko-chan.

00:06:14.550 --> 00:06:16.820
I don't mind, Auntie.

00:06:31.140 --> 00:06:33.520
You should drive your car to school.

00:06:33.520 --> 00:06:36.200
I mean, they spent all that
money on it for you.

00:06:36.200 --> 00:06:39.580
You wouldn't let me drive you
to school even if I offered.

00:06:39.580 --> 00:06:41.830
I like taking the train.

00:06:41.830 --> 00:06:44.200
You always say that.

00:06:45.860 --> 00:06:48.450
Depend on me a little more, will you?

00:06:49.750 --> 00:06:52.050
I'm always depending on you.

00:06:52.050 --> 00:06:55.620
You mean you <i>used</i>
to depend on me.

00:06:57.620 --> 00:07:01.280
Kyoko, being so selfish will
make you lose your appeal.

00:07:01.280 --> 00:07:04.050
I never had any appeal to begin with.

00:07:05.860 --> 00:07:09.480
I have till Sunday to gather the girls, right?

00:07:11.110 --> 00:07:12.000
Yeah.

00:07:12.430 --> 00:07:14.200
I'll call you when I'm ready.

00:07:14.610 --> 00:07:17.090
You take care of the set-up on your side.

00:07:17.090 --> 00:07:18.960
Thanks for walking me to school.

00:07:22.720 --> 00:07:25.740
She really lacks appeal.

00:07:30.760 --> 00:07:32.040
Okudaira-san.

00:07:33.310 --> 00:07:34.860
Do you have a minute?

00:07:35.920 --> 00:07:37.230
A group date!

00:07:37.230 --> 00:07:39.560
You're talking about a group date, right?

00:07:39.560 --> 00:07:42.020
I guess you could call it that...

00:07:42.020 --> 00:07:44.780
Wow, a group date.

00:07:44.780 --> 00:07:47.990
I'll finally make my group date debut!

00:07:48.330 --> 00:07:50.550
You don't need to make such
a big deal about it.

00:07:50.550 --> 00:07:53.610
But there will be college guys there.

00:07:53.610 --> 00:07:56.160
I don't know what to talk to them about!

00:07:56.540 --> 00:08:01.530
My fiancé is organizing it.
I think you'll like him.

00:08:01.720 --> 00:08:05.890
Fiancé... You're engaged already...

00:08:05.890 --> 00:08:08.270
In name only.

00:08:09.180 --> 00:08:12.800
Umm, so the person you like is...?

00:08:13.130 --> 00:08:14.790
Not him.

00:08:16.230 --> 00:08:17.730
It wouldn't be, huh?

00:08:17.730 --> 00:08:20.820
The person I like rejected me.

00:08:20.820 --> 00:08:21.540
Huh?

00:08:24.190 --> 00:08:27.530
So I'm pretty desperate because of it.

00:08:54.040 --> 00:08:58.750
"The only males who will be
allowed are close relatives."

00:08:58.750 --> 00:09:01.680
"Only fiancés will be granted
special permission."

00:09:01.680 --> 00:09:04.320
Wow, only fiancés!

00:09:04.320 --> 00:09:05.450
It's wild, right?

00:09:05.450 --> 00:09:07.660
That's what I'd expect from such
a high-class girls' school!

00:09:07.660 --> 00:09:12.360
But doesn't everyone bring their boyfriends
and say they're their fiancés?

00:09:12.360 --> 00:09:14.250
Exactly!

00:09:14.250 --> 00:09:17.360
Apparently some girls have
a new fiancé each year!

00:09:18.270 --> 00:09:20.320
That's just wrong.

00:09:53.150 --> 00:09:56.450
Most of the country will
be sunny tomorrow.

00:09:56.450 --> 00:09:57.330
Continuing on...

00:10:01.460 --> 00:10:04.120
What in heaven's name are you doing?

00:10:04.470 --> 00:10:07.410
I felt like moving my desk around.

00:10:07.410 --> 00:10:11.710
Do that tomorrow. It's Sunday.

00:10:12.500 --> 00:10:16.180
I'll be done as soon as I put the
things back on my desk.

00:10:24.930 --> 00:10:26.180
OK.

00:10:33.330 --> 00:10:35.860
I'm dead serious.

00:10:40.950 --> 00:10:42.610
Let's go on a date.

00:10:42.610 --> 00:10:43.640
Huh?

00:10:44.180 --> 00:10:46.730
Do you have plans with someone
else on Sunday?

00:10:46.730 --> 00:10:48.200
I don't...

00:10:48.200 --> 00:10:49.460
Then it's decided.

00:10:49.460 --> 00:10:51.750
How's ten o'clock at Kamakura
station sound?

00:10:51.750 --> 00:10:52.920
Sure...

00:10:52.920 --> 00:10:56.480
Manjome-san! Let's go home!

00:11:02.710 --> 00:11:06.030
What should I wear tomorrow?

00:11:11.240 --> 00:11:12.990
Huh?!

00:11:12.990 --> 00:11:14.940
What are you talking about?

00:11:14.940 --> 00:11:16.900
No friggin' way!

00:11:16.900 --> 00:11:19.460
I'll never talk to you again if you do that!

00:11:19.460 --> 00:11:21.370
Give it up.

00:11:21.370 --> 00:11:23.400
I'll tell Dad.

00:11:23.780 --> 00:11:26.030
What do you think Dad'll do if he finds out?

00:11:26.540 --> 00:11:27.880
What is it?

00:11:28.520 --> 00:11:30.180
Something going on?

00:11:30.180 --> 00:11:32.070
It's nothing!

00:11:32.850 --> 00:11:33.800
OK.

00:11:34.320 --> 00:11:36.730
Don't yell then.

00:11:36.730 --> 00:11:38.160
R-Right...

00:11:38.160 --> 00:11:41.040
He's ten times tougher than I am.

00:11:41.040 --> 00:11:42.150
What's it gonna be?

00:11:46.580 --> 00:11:49.560
I put your medicine on the table.

00:11:49.560 --> 00:11:51.970
Oh, thank you.

00:11:51.970 --> 00:11:56.260
You're no spring chicken
anymore. Take it easy.

00:11:56.260 --> 00:11:57.320
Right.

00:11:57.580 --> 00:11:59.530
Is Fumi still asleep?

00:11:59.530 --> 00:12:01.570
She left a while ago.

00:12:01.570 --> 00:12:03.900
Oh. Out shopping?

00:12:03.900 --> 00:12:06.140
Who knows. Maybe she had a date.

00:12:08.410 --> 00:12:11.710
Who's the guy? She didn't say she
needs a cellphone, did she?

00:12:11.710 --> 00:12:15.010
No... You worry too much.

00:12:15.010 --> 00:12:17.380
You aren't worried about her date?

00:12:17.380 --> 00:12:20.510
I'd be more worried if she
<i>wasn't</i> dating.

00:12:29.040 --> 00:12:31.550
Okudaira-san, over here.

00:12:33.770 --> 00:12:36.120
Sorry I'm late!

00:12:36.120 --> 00:12:40.060
It's fine. We got here early.

00:12:40.060 --> 00:12:45.160
We're still waiting for someone.
He's really bad at being on time.

00:12:45.160 --> 00:12:47.500
This is Ko Sawanoi-san.

00:12:47.500 --> 00:12:50.560
He's my fiancé. I told you about him.

00:12:50.560 --> 00:12:51.790
Nice to meet you.

00:12:51.790 --> 00:12:55.250
N-Nice to meet you! I'm Akira Okudaira.

00:13:36.890 --> 00:13:38.460
Is there anyone you've been seeing?

00:13:38.740 --> 00:13:41.660
Huh? Why ask me that all of a sudden?

00:13:41.660 --> 00:13:43.920
I was curious if there was.

00:13:43.920 --> 00:13:47.320
There isn't...

00:13:53.330 --> 00:13:55.080
Let's go look at the ocean.

00:13:55.080 --> 00:13:57.340
Huh? The ocean...?

00:13:57.620 --> 00:13:59.480
I have a secret place.

00:13:59.480 --> 00:14:02.270
We should have it all to
ourselves right now.

00:14:13.070 --> 00:14:17.150
This place fills up with people when
the hydrangeas are in bloom.

00:14:19.640 --> 00:14:21.880
This is the first time I've come here.

00:14:24.140 --> 00:14:26.420
You've got a pretty name, Fumi.

00:14:27.650 --> 00:14:29.530
Thank you.

00:14:29.850 --> 00:14:31.000
Fumi-chan.

00:14:32.750 --> 00:14:33.740
Fumi?

00:14:37.600 --> 00:14:38.750
Yes...

00:14:39.840 --> 00:14:42.290
Let's go out again.

00:14:49.320 --> 00:14:50.400
Weirdo.

00:14:50.710 --> 00:14:52.030
What's wrong?

00:14:52.030 --> 00:14:54.270
I think we're being followed.

00:14:54.270 --> 00:14:55.820
No way...

00:14:55.820 --> 00:14:58.350
Some creepy looking guy in sunglasses.

00:14:58.350 --> 00:15:02.250
He's about our age. I've seen
him three times today.

00:15:02.250 --> 00:15:03.670
Sure you're not imagining things?

00:15:03.670 --> 00:15:09.700
No, he was just staring over here the whole time,
without moving, while I was ordering the food.

00:15:09.700 --> 00:15:12.230
Sure he wasn't checking out
the girl who works here?

00:15:12.230 --> 00:15:13.960
Eww, a stalker?

00:15:13.960 --> 00:15:18.220
I'm sorry! That's my big brother!

00:15:18.740 --> 00:15:21.530
I told him not to, but he came anyway.

00:15:22.130 --> 00:15:24.840
And after you were so kind to invite me...

00:15:24.840 --> 00:15:27.340
I told him he'd better not follow me...

00:15:27.340 --> 00:15:29.380
But he ignored me.

00:15:30.500 --> 00:15:32.000
I hate him!

00:15:33.610 --> 00:15:37.270
Die, you idiot, idiot, idiot!

00:15:35.790 --> 00:15:38.490
Don't do that, Akira! Those are hard!

00:15:41.250 --> 00:15:44.010
You're unbelievable! You ruined everything!

00:15:44.010 --> 00:15:45.910
They all thought I'm such a weirdo!

00:15:45.910 --> 00:15:49.010
What do you enjoy about embarrassing
your little sister?!

00:15:49.320 --> 00:15:51.220
That's just it...

00:15:51.220 --> 00:15:55.440
I can't stomach the idea of some guy taking
my little sister home with him...

00:15:55.440 --> 00:15:56.960
What an idiot.

00:15:56.960 --> 00:15:58.420
What?

00:15:58.420 --> 00:16:01.690
That's why you can't get a girlfriend!

00:16:01.690 --> 00:16:04.600
Worry about yourself instead
of me for once!

00:16:05.840 --> 00:16:06.920
As long as I have you-

00:16:06.920 --> 00:16:08.780
Stop saying that, you creep!

00:16:10.860 --> 00:16:15.690
Do you think you can stop now?
The neighbors will get the wrong idea.

00:16:17.170 --> 00:16:18.130
Sorry.

00:16:24.310 --> 00:16:27.730
Come on, cheer up already.

00:16:39.440 --> 00:16:42.480
That girl, Ikumi-san, is pretty sexy, huh?

00:16:43.570 --> 00:16:48.100
Sucks to be you. She's got
a great fiancé already.

00:16:48.100 --> 00:16:50.910
You said yourself that it's in name only.

00:16:50.910 --> 00:16:53.810
Oh, so you're after Ikumi-san now.

00:16:53.810 --> 00:16:55.230
No, I'm not.

00:16:55.710 --> 00:16:59.240
I'm saying that she might be after you.

00:16:59.240 --> 00:17:01.620
Huh? N-No way!

00:17:01.620 --> 00:17:03.520
Can you say that for certain?

00:17:03.520 --> 00:17:07.590
If it's really in name only, I wouldn't be surprised
if the engagement gets called off.

00:17:09.580 --> 00:17:12.070
What an interesting girl.

00:17:12.070 --> 00:17:14.250
She's cute, right?

00:17:14.250 --> 00:17:18.220
I guess it makes sense she'd cry,
since her brother followed her.

00:17:18.220 --> 00:17:21.270
They ended up going home together.

00:17:24.890 --> 00:17:27.180
But she really is a cute one.

00:17:30.360 --> 00:17:33.150
Are you back, Fumi?

00:17:46.120 --> 00:17:47.130
Fumi?

00:17:49.170 --> 00:17:51.070
Let's go out again.

00:17:58.150 --> 00:17:59.010
Here you go.

00:18:00.530 --> 00:18:02.400
Read it well.

00:18:02.400 --> 00:18:05.510
Don't skim it just because you
aren't going to be on stage.

00:18:05.510 --> 00:18:07.030
I-I won't!

00:18:07.030 --> 00:18:11.480
Kawasaki-sempai, I have something
to ask the club president.

00:18:11.810 --> 00:18:14.360
She's in Kagami-sensei's office right now.

00:18:14.360 --> 00:18:16.780
She'll be back real soon, I bet.

00:18:18.090 --> 00:18:19.810
Faculty Room

00:18:20.920 --> 00:18:23.680
Oh, the script is ready.

00:18:23.680 --> 00:18:26.920
Are preparations for the play going well?

00:18:26.920 --> 00:18:29.150
It's coming along.

00:18:29.150 --> 00:18:33.110
I'm sorry I haven't been able
to help the club out at all.

00:18:34.010 --> 00:18:36.620
I never expected you to.

00:18:36.620 --> 00:18:40.680
Sensei, we're totally fine,
with or without you.

00:18:41.200 --> 00:18:42.420
Sorry.

00:18:42.420 --> 00:18:45.420
I-I was just joking!

00:18:45.420 --> 00:18:46.540
Right.

00:18:46.870 --> 00:18:49.540
I guess I was a little sarcastic, too.

00:18:49.540 --> 00:18:50.550
Right.

00:18:52.690 --> 00:18:57.350
We asked Sugimoto to guest star.
She's going to play Heathcliff.

00:18:58.050 --> 00:19:00.690
Oh, is she doing well?

00:19:00.690 --> 00:19:04.530
Yes. She's getting more
handsome by the day.

00:19:05.700 --> 00:19:07.410
Handsome, huh?

00:19:08.530 --> 00:19:10.680
Is she in the drama club at her school?

00:19:10.680 --> 00:19:12.480
She's playing sports, actually.

00:19:12.480 --> 00:19:14.790
I guess she's the captain
of the basketball team.

00:19:14.790 --> 00:19:16.600
Wow, impressive.

00:19:16.600 --> 00:19:19.990
She's so good at everything she does.

00:19:21.080 --> 00:19:22.850
That's true.

00:19:30.760 --> 00:19:32.340
OK, thanks.

00:19:32.900 --> 00:19:35.800
Thanks for being so patient with me.

00:19:35.800 --> 00:19:39.420
So, you're done with the basketball
team now, huh?

00:19:39.420 --> 00:19:40.480
What a shame.

00:19:40.480 --> 00:19:44.110
She's here all the time, so
don't let your guard down.

00:19:44.110 --> 00:19:46.690
She's a really aggressive recruiter.

00:19:46.690 --> 00:19:49.310
I'll recruit her out of here first, then.

00:19:51.790 --> 00:19:54.720
Manjome-san, let's go to the library.

00:20:01.010 --> 00:20:03.100
Steel shelves aren't bad,

00:20:03.100 --> 00:20:06.240
but wood ones have a certain
elegance to them.

00:20:06.890 --> 00:20:09.570
Fujigaya's library is really pretty.

00:20:09.570 --> 00:20:13.620
Indeed. It's like "The Library".

00:20:13.970 --> 00:20:17.520
I get why Achan chose Fujigaya now.

00:20:17.520 --> 00:20:20.210
Oh, Achan is...

00:20:22.100 --> 00:20:25.820
There's a "Master of the Library" at Fujigaya...

00:20:26.240 --> 00:20:28.290
"Master of the Library"?

00:20:29.910 --> 00:20:36.990
Some teacher was messing around and called a
girl who loves books that, and the name stuck.

00:20:38.060 --> 00:20:40.330
That's great.

00:20:41.370 --> 00:20:43.130
Why do you have tears in your eyes?

00:20:43.390 --> 00:20:49.010
Please don't move in so close to
me while I'm still not ready.

00:20:50.620 --> 00:20:53.090
All right, to get ready...

00:20:53.090 --> 00:20:54.240
Huh?

00:20:55.170 --> 00:20:56.600
Take a deep breath.

00:21:03.290 --> 00:21:06.650
Surrounded by the steel
shelves in the library...

00:21:06.650 --> 00:21:11.260
That was where Sempai and
I shared our first kiss.

00:21:11.930 --> 00:21:14.910
Rise and Shine

00:23:34.850 --> 00:23:39.860
See you next time.
